                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1775fc90-7878-4acd-b66d-1adeb65e629f",
                        "source_entry_id": "e5dc5d9b-5eb8-3964-baec-700b4b3eeade",
                        "source_sense_id": "3b9d4d53-9879-3b56-9fe0-4ce36d6e072f",
                        "target_lang_word": "irene",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "irene",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "56dc83af-adf9-3603-9ca5-637ef8140acd",
                                        "entry_id": "44f87f84-f12c-3205-87df-38198c4c015f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The hydrocarbon formed by dehydration of an irone."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5df45768-d188-4503-b57f-af2d78109329",
                                                "sense_id": "56dc83af-adf9-3603-9ca5-637ef8140acd",
                                                "text": "The configurations around the double bond in the side chain are based on considerations of the Raman spectra, dielectric constants, etc., and on comparatively small differences in reactivity; for example, neo-α-irone is converted into irene less readily than α-irone, but forms an oxime more rapidly; …"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "27fe0d5d-81fa-4b22-9fb3-2b3036e7c5db",
                                                "sense_id": "56dc83af-adf9-3603-9ca5-637ef8140acd",
                                                "text": "Ruzicka and his co-workers showed that the hydrocarbon irene, obtained on reduction of irone with red phosphorus/iodine, had the structure shown and this was confirmed by synthesis [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f1231dc-0fb5-4480-afd4-31b7d164212c",
                                                "sense_id": "56dc83af-adf9-3603-9ca5-637ef8140acd",
                                                "text": "Practically no isomerization of ɑ- or γ-irone into β-irone, or of γ-irone into ɑ-irone takes place; nor is irene formed from the irones."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
